-- title:
--   Integrality over K[j(q)] inside the modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring, $K$ a field and $res : O \to K$ a ring homomorphism, and let $N$ be a positive natural number. Let $Q$ be a polynomial in one variable with coefficients in $\mathrm{Polynomial}\ O$, i.e. a two-variable polynomial over $O$, and let $z$ be a formal Laurent series over $O$ (a Hahn series over $\mathbb{Z}$ with coefficients in $O$). Assume $z$ is obtained from $Q$ by first applying, coefficientwise, the ring homomorphism $\mathrm{Polynomial}\ O \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ O$ that evaluates at `jqModC O` and then evaluating the resulting polynomial at `jqNModC O N`; here `jqModC O` is the series $\mathrm{single}(-1,1)$ times the image over $O$ of the integral power series `jNum` $=$ `eisenstein4`$^3 \cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv` (the $q$-expansion of $j$, with leading coefficient $1$ in degree $-1$), and `jqNModC O N` is its image under `qExpand O N`, the ring endomorphism multiplying all exponents by $N$ (so $z = Q(j(q), j(q^N))$). Assume moreover, as a hypothesis, that the coefficientwise image `coeffMap res z` of $z$ under $res$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the intermediate field $K(j(q), j(q^N))$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ K$ generated over $K$ by `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`. The conclusion is that `coeffMap res z`, viewed as an element of this intermediate field, is integral over the $K$-subalgebra of that field generated by the single element `jqModC K` of it.
--
--   This is the form, internal to the field $K(j(q),j(q^N))$, of the classical integrality of $j(N\tau)$ over $\mathbb{Z}[j]$ via the modular polynomial $\Phi_N$: the ambient integrality over $K[j(q)]$ inside the Laurent series is transferred along the inclusion of the intermediate field, the generating element being the same. The membership hypothesis is not derived here; it is to be provided by the corresponding membership statement. It is used in the study of places and specialisations of the modular curve and in the mod $p$ theory of forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isIntegral_adjoin_mk_coeffMap.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JqCoeff

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.isIntegral_adjoin_mk_coeffMap {O : Type*} [CommRing O] {K : Type*}
    [Field K] (res : O →+* K) (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (Q : Polynomial (Polynomial O))
    (z : LaurentSeries O)
    (hzrep : z = ((Q.map (Polynomial.aeval (jqModC O)).toRingHom).eval (jqNModC O N)))
    (hmem : coeffMap res z ∈ modularFunctionFieldC K N) :
    IsIntegral
      (Algebra.adjoin K ({(⟨jqModC K, jqModC_mem K N⟩ : modularFunctionFieldC K N)} :
        Set (modularFunctionFieldC K N)))
      (⟨coeffMap res z, hmem⟩ : modularFunctionFieldC K N) := by sorry
